-- #1292 (S0) regression: `eval.runtimeTypeTag` tagged a `VCon` by its BARE
-- constructor name through the PROGRAM-GLOBAL `ctorToTypeRef`, so two modules
-- declaring a same-named constructor collapsed to one entry and every value of
-- the loser's type was tagged with the winner's TYPE — dispatching to the wrong
-- impl silently, at exit 0.
--
-- Both lines below construct a `Box`, but from DIFFERENT modules' `Box`:
--   * `mkA 7`   is built inside amodl, so it is amodl's `Box` : TA -> "amod"
--   * `Box 5`   is bmodl's `Box` (the only `Box` this module imports) : TB -> "bmod"
-- Two lines, not one, so the fixture fails whichever way the table collapses:
-- a first-wins table gets the second line wrong, a last-wins table the first.
--
-- 🚨 GOLDEN HAND-WRITTEN FROM THE SEMANTICS ABOVE, never captured — capturing at
-- the buggy base would have enshrined `amod\namod` as "correct" forever.
import labeliface.{Label, label}
import amodl.{TA, mkA}
import bmodl.{TB, Box}

main =
  println (label (mkA 7))
  println (label (Box 5))
